  appears_when all: { place: [:sealed_hab] }
  summary "A balance is a counterweighted passenger and freight lift rigged through the dead vertical shafts of ring fragments — two cars on one line over a salvaged wheel, balanced so a hand crew can move real loads. Rekindling engineering at its plainest, and the spine of vertical life in the habs."
  function "Moves people and freight through ring-era shafts on balanced paired cars"
  classes "Hand-wound neighborhood pairs, treadwheel freight balances, and the long compound rigs that ladder a whole fragment in stages"
  capacity "A neighborhood pair trades four passengers against ballast; freight rigs rate by the counter-car and post the number at the gate"
  operating_limit "Runs at the pace of its winders and banks against its brakes; a balance is set for its posted load and a heavy surprise arrives at the bottom quickly"

  descriptive_identity(
    appearance: "Two open cars on one certified line over a salvaged head-wheel, running in a " \
                "ring-era shaft whose original fittings stand dark around the new rig. The gate " \
                "posts the rated load in paint refreshed yearly, and the brake lever wears its " \
                "handle smooth.",
    working: "The cars balance each other: passengers down winds ballast up, freight up rides " \
             "water-cans down, and the winder's craft is loading the pair so the wheel wants to " \
